#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This module of the &kde; &systemsettings; allows you to select customization "
"options that depend on the region of the world that you happen to live in. "
"There are seven different tabs in this module, each of which is described in "
"detail in the following sections."
msgstr ""
"Ovaj modul &kde; &systemsettings; omogućava da odaberete opcije "
"prilagođavanja u zavisnosti regije u kojoj živite. Postoji sedam različitih "
"tab-ova u ovom modulu, svaki je objašnjen detaljno u slijedećim dijelovima."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In most cases, you can simply select the country and the language, and the "
"other options will be set in an appropriate manner."
msgstr ""
"U većini slučajeva, možete jednostavno odabrate zemlju i jezik, i ostale "
"opcije će se postaviti na odgovarajuće postavke."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the tabs of this module you can see a preview of what the settings "
"look like. In addition to positive and negative numbers, you can see how "
"positive and negative currency values, long and short dates, and times are "
"displayed. When you change any of the settings, the preview shows the "
"effects of the changes before you apply them."
msgstr ""
"Ispod tab-ova ovog modula možete vidjeti pregled kako podešavanja izgledaju. "
"Kao dodatak pozitivnim i negativnim brojevima, možete vidjeti kako su "
"prikazane pozitivne i negativne vrijednosti valuta,daleke i kratke datume, i "
"vrijeme je prikazano,. Kada promjeni bilo koji od ovih postavki, pregled vam "
"pokazuje promjene prije nego ih primjenite."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each setting option in the various tabs has an individual "
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"oxygen-22x22-document-"
"revert.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></inlinemediaobject> default "
"button which is activated whenever that setting is different to your country "
"default value. Clicking on the button will restore only that setting to your "
"Country default."
msgstr ""
"Svako podešavanje opcija u raznim tab-ovima ima individualni "
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"oxygen-22x22-document-"
"revert.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></inlinemediaobject> zadano "
"dugme koja se aktivira kada god je to podešavanje drugačije od zadane "
"vrijednosti vaše zemlje. Pristikom na to dugme će se vratiti samo to "
"podešavanje na zadane postavke za Vašu zemlju."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Country"
msgstr "Država"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this tab you can select the country or region that you want to use."
msgstr ""
"U ovom tab-u moćete izabrati zemlju ili region koji želite da koristite."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Country</guilabel> drop down box contains the list of "
"available countries and will initially show your currently selected country. "
"If the selection shows <quote>System Country</quote> then you have not set a "
"country and are defaulting to the Country set by the system, which will also "
"be shown. Changing the country will automatically change the settings to the "
"defaults for that country, except were you have set your own settings which "
"will be left unchanged. You can easily see where your personal settings "
"differ from the country settings by looking at the Default button next to "
"the individual setting. If the button is enabled then your personal setting "
"is different and you can click on the button to restore the country setting "
"for that option only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "Languages"
msgstr "Jezici"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this tab you can set your preferred languages for the &kde; Workspace and "
"Applications to be displayed in."
msgstr ""
"U ovom tabu možete odrediti vaš prioritetan jezik za &kde; Mjesto za rad i "
"aplikacije da budu prikazane."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; Workspace and Applications are written in American English and are "
"translated into many different languages by teams of volunteers. These "
"translations need to be installed first before you can choose to use them. "
"The list of <guilabel>Available Languages</guilabel> shows what KDE "
"translations are installed and available on your system. If the language you "
"want to use is not shown in this list then you will need to install it using "
"the usual method for your system. Your system may have enabled the "
"<guilabel>Install more languages</guilabel> button to make this easy for you."
msgstr ""
"&kde; Radni prostor i aplikacije su napisane u Američkom engleskom i one se "
"prevode na mnoge jezike u timovima volontera. Ovi prevodi moraju biti "
"instalirani prvo prije nego ih odlučite koristiti.Lista <guilabel>dostupnih "
"jezika</guilabel> pokazuje koji KDE prevodi su instalirani i koji su mogući "
"na vašem sistemu.Ako jezik koji vi želite koristiti nije na listi, onda ga "
"vi morate instalirati korišteći standardnu metodu za vaš sistem.Vaš sistem "
"je možda omogućio<guilabel>Instaliraj još jezika</guilabel> dugme da bi bilo "
"lakše za vas."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Preferred Languages</guilabel> list shows the languages that "
"will be used when displaying the &kde; Workspace and Applications. Because "
"not all of the KDE Workspace and Applications may be translated into every "
"language &kde; will try to find suitable translations for you by working "
"down the <guilabel>Preferred Languages</guilabel> list until it finds a "
"translation. If none of your preferred languages have a required translation "
"then the original American English will be used."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Preferirani jezici</guilabel> lista pokazuje jezike koji će biti "
"korišteni u prikazivanju &kde; Radnog prostors i aplikacije. Nije sve od KDE "
"Radnog prostora i aplikacija prevedeno na sve jezike pa će &kde; pokušati "
"naći odgovarajući jezik korišteći<guilabel>Preferirani jezici</guilabel> "
"listu dok ne nađe prevod. Ako nijedan od vaših prioritetnih jezika nema "
"prevoda, onda će se koristiti original Američki engleski."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can add a language to the <guilabel>Preferred Languages</guilabel> list "
"by selecting it in the <guilabel>Available Languages</guilabel> and then "
"clicking on the Add arrow button. You can remove a language from the "
"<guilabel>Preferred Languages</guilabel> list by selecting it and then "
"clicking on the Remove arrow button. You can change the order of preference "
"in the <guilabel>Preferred Languages</guilabel> list by selecting a language "
"and clicking on the Up or Down arrow button."
msgstr ""
"Jezik možete dodati u <guilabel>Preferirani jezici</guilabel> listu "
"označavajući ih u <guilabel>Dostupni jezici</guilabel> i onda klik na dugme "
"Dodaj strelice. Možete izbrisati jezik iz liste <guilabel>Preferiranih "
"jezila</guilabel> list označavajući ih i klik na dugme za brisanje s "
"strelicom . Raspored možete promjeniti na  <guilabel>Preferirani jezici</"
"guilabel> listi označavajući ih i klik na Gore ili Dole dugme za strelicu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only languages listed in <guilabel>Preferred Languages</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Available Languages</guilabel> will be offered as options for "
"<guilabel>Primary language</guilabel> and <guilabel>Fallback language</"
"guilabel> in the <guilabel>Switch Application Language</guilabel> dialog of "
"the <guimenu>Help</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""
"Samo jezici izlistani u  <guilabel>Preferred Languages</guilabel> "
"i<guilabel>Available Languages</guilabel>bit će ponuđeni kao opcija za "
"<guilabel>Primary language</guilabel> i<guilabel>Fallback language</"
"guilabel> u  <guilabel>Switch Application Language</guilabel> dialog of the "
"<guimenu>Help</guimenu> menu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Language and Country/Region are independent settings. Changing a language "
"does <emphasis>not</emphasis> automatically change the settings for numbers, "
"currency &etc; to the corresponding country or region. It will only change "
"the language used in displaying dates, such as month names."
msgstr ""
"Jezik i Država/Regija su odvojena podešavanja. Mjenjajući jezik <emphasis></"
"emphasis> se ne mjenjaju automatski podešavanja za brojeve,valute&etc;za "
"određenu zemlju ili regiju. Samo će promjeniti jezik kao kada npr. pokazuje "
"imena mjeseca."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "Numbers"
msgstr "Brojevi"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, you can select options for how numbers are displayed. The "
"defaults are selected automatically based on the country which is currently "
"selected."
msgstr ""
"Na ovom tab-u, možete odabrati opciju koliko brojeva želite da se prikažu. "
"Zadane postavke su odabrane automatski na osnovu zemlje koju ste izabrali."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the first drop down box you can define the <guilabel>Digit grouping</"
"guilabel> used to display numbers."
msgstr ""
"U prvoj padajućoj listi možete definisati <guilabel>Grupisanje cifara</"
"guilabel>korišteno za prikazivanje brojeva."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Group separator</guilabel> text box you can type the "
"character that you want to use to separate groups of digits in numbers, "
"usually a <userinput>.</userinput> or a <userinput>,</userinput>. You should "
"ensure that this value is different to the <guilabel>Decimal separator</"
"guilabel> setting. The drop-down box provides a list of common values to "
"choose from."
msgstr ""
"U <guilabel>Separator grupa</guilabel> tekstualnom okviru unijeti znakove "
"koje želite da koristite da podijelite grupe   <userinput>.</userinput> ili  "
"<userinput>,</userinput>Morate se uvjeriti da je ta vrijednost drugačija od "
"<guilabel>Decimalni separator</guilabel> podešavanja. Padajući meni "
"omogućava da izaberete iz liste zajedničkih vrijednosti."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Decimal separator</guilabel> text box you can type the "
"character that you want to use to separate the decimal portion of numbers, "
"usually a <userinput>.</userinput> or a <userinput>,</userinput>. You should "
"ensure that this value is different to the <guilabel>Group separator</"
"guilabel> setting. The drop-down box provides a list of common values to "
"choose from."
msgstr ""
"U <guilabel>Group separator</guilabel> prostoru za text unijeti znakove koje "
"želite da koristite da podijelite grupe   <userinput>.</userinput> ili  "
"<userinput>,</userinput>Morate se uvjeriti da je ta vrijednost drugačija od "
"<guilabel>Decimal separator</guilabel> podešavanja. Padajući meni omogućava "
"da izaberete od liste zajedničkih vrijednosti."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Decimal places</guilabel> spin box you can set the number "
"of decimal places displayed for numeric values, &ie; the number of digits "
"<emphasis>after</emphasis> the decimal separator."
msgstr ""
"U <guilabel>Decimal places</guilabel> spin box-u možete odrediti broj "
"decimalnih mjesta za prikazivanje za prikazivanje numeričkih vrijednosti,"
"&ie; the number of digits <emphasis>after</emphasis>  za decimalni razmak."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Positive sign</guilabel> text box you can type the "
"character that you want to use to indicate positive numbers. You should "
"ensure that this value is different to the <guilabel>Negative sign</"
"guilabel> setting. The drop-down box provides a list of common values to "
"choose from. This value may also be used for monetary values depending on "
"the <guilabel>Positive format</guilabel> selected in the <guilabel>Money</"
"guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Negative sign</guilabel> text box you can type the "
"character that you want to use to indicate negative numbers. You should "
"ensure that this value is different to the <guilabel>Positive sign</"
"guilabel> setting. The drop-down box provides a list of common values to "
"choose from. This value may also be used for monetary values depending on "
"the <guilabel>Negative format</guilabel> selected in the <guilabel>Money</"
"guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Digit set</guilabel> drop down box lists digit sets which may "
"be used instead of Arabic digits when displaying numbers. If you select a "
"digit set other than Arabic, it will be applied only to numbers which appear "
"in a language context that uses that digit set while Arabic digits are still "
"going to be used elsewhere, &eg; Arabic-Indic digits will be applied to "
"Arabic but not to American English."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that digit grouping, group separator, decimal separator, decimal "
"places, positive format, negative format and the digit set used to display "
"monetary values has to be set separately on the <guilabel>Money</guilabel> "
"tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "Money"
msgstr "Novac"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, you can select options for how monetary values are displayed. "
"The defaults are selected automatically based on the country which is "
"currently selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Currency</guilabel> drop-down box you can choose the "
"currency you want to use when displaying monetary values. This will default "
"to the main currency in use in your selected country. You can choose a "
"different currency from the drop-down box, which displays the names of all "
"available currencies their ISO 4217 standard Currency Code. The currencies "
"used in your selected country are listed at the top, followed by all the "
"other currencies. Changing the currency will also update the "
"<guilabel>Currency symbol</guilabel> to use the default symbol for that "
"currency, but no other format settings will be changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Currency symbol</guilabel> drop-down box you can choose the "
"currency symbol you want to use when displaying monetary values. This will "
"default to the usual symbol of the currency you have selected in the "
"<guilabel>Currency</guilabel> drop-down box. This will only allow you to "
"select a valid currency symbol for the currency code to prevent inconsistent "
"choices, such as choosing US Dollars but showing the Pound Sterling symbol £ "
"instead. This setting will automatically be changed when you change the "
"<guilabel>Currency</guilabel> setting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the next drop down box you can define the <guilabel>Digit grouping</"
"guilabel> used to display monetary values."
msgstr ""
"U slijedećem padajućem meniu možete definisati <guilabel>Digit grouping</"
"guilabel> koristi se da prikaze monetarne vrijednosti."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Group separator</guilabel> text box you can type the "
"character that you want to use to separate groups of digits in monetary "
"values, usually a <userinput>.</userinput> or a <userinput>,</userinput>. "
"You should ensure that this value is different to the <guilabel>Decimal "
"separator</guilabel> setting. The drop-down box provides a list of common "
"values to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Decimal separator</guilabel> text box you can type the "
"character that you want to use to separate the decimal portion of monetary "
"values, usually a <userinput>.</userinput> or a <userinput>,</userinput>. "
"You should ensure that this value is different to the <guilabel>Group "
"separator</guilabel> setting. The drop-down box provides a list of common "
"values to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Decimal places</guilabel> spin box you can set the number "
"of decimal places displayed for monetary values, &ie; the number of digits "
"<emphasis>after</emphasis> the decimal separator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Positive format</guilabel> drop-down box you can select how "
"you want positive monetary values to be displayed. The drop-down box "
"displays a list of four sample formats that you can choose from, combining "
"the options for where the <guilabel>Currency symbol</guilabel> and the "
"numeric value <guilabel>Positive sign</guilabel> are displayed. You can also "
"choose to replace the numeric value <guilabel>Positive sign</guilabel> with "
"brackets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Negative format</guilabel> drop-down box you can select how "
"you want negative monetary values to be displayed. The drop-down box "
"displays a list of ten sample formats that you can choose from, combining "
"the options for where the <guilabel>Currency symbol</guilabel> and the "
"numeric value <guilabel>Negative sign</guilabel> are displayed. You can also "
"choose to replace the numeric value <guilabel>Negative sign</guilabel> with "
"brackets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Digit set</guilabel> drop down box lists digit sets which may "
"be used instead of Arabic digits when displaying money. If you select a "
"digit set other than Arabic, it will be applied only to numbers which appear "
"in a language context that uses that digit set while Arabic digits are still "
"going to be used elsewhere, &eg; Arabic-Indic digits will be applied to "
"Arabic but not to American English."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that digit grouping, group separator, decimal separator, decimal "
"places, positive sign, negative sign and the digit set used to display "
"numeric values has to be set separately on the <guilabel>Numbers</guilabel> "
"tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "Calendar"
msgstr "Kalendar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, you can select options for how calendar information is "
"displayed. The defaults are selected automatically based on the country "
"which is currently selected."
msgstr ""
"Na ovom tabu, možete izabrati opcije kako kalendarske informacije su "
"prikazane. Zadane vrijednosti su određene automatski na osnovu države koja "
"je odabrana."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Calendar system</guilabel> drop-down box you can choose the "
"calendar system to be used when displaying or inputting dates. This will "
"default to the main calendar system in use in your selected country, usually "
"the Gregorian calendar. Changing the calendar system will also update the "
"various weekday name drop-down combos with the names of days of the week in "
"the new calendar system, will enable or disable the <guilabel>Use Common "
"Era</guilabel> tick box and may change the value of the <guilabel>Short year "
"window</guilabel> setting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that the Gregorian calendar used is a hybrid of the Julian calendar up "
"to Thursday 4 October 1582 and the Gregorian calendar from Friday 15 October "
"1582, leaving a <quote>gap</quote> of ten <quote>missing</quote> days. We "
"are aware this conversion date is not factually correct for all countries, "
"however this is how Qt have chosen to implement the Gregorian calendar and "
"we wish to remain consistent with them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have selected the Gregorian calendar system then the <guilabel>Use "
"Common Era</guilabel> tick box will be enabled. This allows you to choose to "
"use the Common Era (CE/BCE) instead of the Christian Era (AD/BC) when "
"displaying and inputting dates. See the <guilabel>Date &amp; Time</guilabel> "
"tab for how to set this up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Short year window</guilabel> option is only used when you "
"choose to use a short two digit year format (YY) in the <guilabel>Long date "
"format</guilabel> or <guilabel>Short date format</guilabel> settings in the "
"<guilabel>Date &amp; Time</guilabel> tab. When inputting a short year value, "
"&eg; 10, the system must guess what century that year falls in. By setting "
"the <guilabel>Short year window</guilabel> you tell the system how you want "
"the short year to be interpreted, &eg; whether 50 is interpreted as 1950 or "
"2050. This window can be set differently for each calendar system as they "
"all use different epochs (start dates). For example, the Hebrew calendar is "
"into its 58th century (2010 Gregorian is roughly 5771 Hebrew), so may use a "
"window of 5750 to 5850."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Week number system</guilabel> option determines how the week "
"number will be calculated. There are four options available:"
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Broj sedmice</guilabel> opcija određuje kako brojevi sedmice će "
"biti računati. Imaju 4 opcije:"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "ISO Week"
msgstr "ISO Sedmica"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the ISO standard Week Number. This will always use Monday as the first "
"day of the ISO week. This is the most commonly used system."
msgstr ""
"Koristi Iso standard broj sedmice.Uvijek će koristiti ponedjeljak kao prvi "
"dan ISO sedmice. Ovo je naupotrebljaviji sistem."

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full First Week"
msgstr "Puna prva sedmica"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first week of the year starts on the first occurrence of the "
"<emphasis>First day of the week</emphasis>, and lasts for seven days. Any "
"days before Week 1 are considered part of the last week of the previous "
"year. This system is most commonly used in the USA."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "Partial First Week"
msgstr "Parcijalna prva sedmica"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first week starts on the first day of the year. The second week of the "
"year starts on the first occurrence of the <emphasis>First day of the week</"
"emphasis>, and lasts for seven days. The first week may not contain seven "
"days."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simple Week"
msgstr "Prosta sedmica"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first week starts on the first day of the year and lasts seven days, "
"with all new weeks starting on the same weekday as the first day of the year."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>First day of week</guilabel> drop-down box you can choose "
"which weekday is considered the first day of the week. This value is often "
"used when displaying calendar tables to determine which day is listed first."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>First working day of week</guilabel> drop-down box you can "
"choose which weekday is considered the first working day of the week. This "
"value is often used when displaying calendar tables to determine when the "
"weekend is."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Last working day of week</guilabel> drop-down box you can "
"choose which weekday is considered the last working day of the week. This "
"value is often used when displaying calendar tables to determine when the "
"weekend is."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:419
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Week day for special religious observance</guilabel> drop-"
"down box you can choose which weekday is regularly used for special "
"religious observances. This value is often used when displaying calendar "
"tables to <quote>red letter</quote> a certain day. If you do not have any "
"particular weekday for religious observance then you can choose the "
"<parameter>None / None in particular</parameter> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid "Date &amp; Time"
msgstr "Datum &amp; Vrijeme"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, you can select options for how date and time values are input "
"or displayed. The defaults are selected automatically based on the country "
"which is currently selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Time format</guilabel> text box you can enter the format "
"that you want to use to input and display times. The format entered is a "
"combination of special codes representing time components and literal text "
"used to separate the time components. The special time component codes are "
"listed below. You can set the format to any combination of time components "
"you like, but you should always include at least an hour and minutes portion "
"to allow you to input times that are not ambiguous. The drop-down box "
"provides a list of common time formats in your currently selected language "
"to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>HH</parameter> - The hour as a decimal number using a 24-hour "
"clock (00-23)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>HH</parameter> -Sat kao decimalni broj koristi 24h sat(00-23)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:457
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>hH</parameter> - The hour as a decimal number using a 24-hour "
"clock (0-23)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>hH</parameter> -Sat kao decimalni broj koristi sat u obliku "
"24sati.(0-23)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>PH</parameter> - The hour as a decimal number using a 12-hour "
"clock (01-12)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>hH</parameter> -Sat kao decimalni broj koristi sat u obliku "
"12sati(01-12)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>pH</parameter> - The hour as a decimal number using a 12-hour "
"clock (1-12)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>hH</parameter> -Sat kao decimalni broj koristi sat u obliku "
"12sati.(1-12)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>MM</parameter> - The minutes as a decimal number (00-59)."
msgstr "<parameter>MM</parameter> - Minute kao decimalni broj (00-59)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>SS</parameter> - The seconds as a decimal number (00-59)."
msgstr "<parameter>MM</parameter> - Sekunde kao decimalni broj (00-59)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>AMPM</parameter> - Either 'AM' or 'PM' according to the given "
"time value. Noon is treated as 'PM' and midnight as 'AM'. You should always "
"include this code if you are using the 12-hour clock codes <parameter>PH</"
"parameter> or <parameter>pH</parameter> to prevent ambiguity when entering "
"times."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>AM symbol</guilabel> text box you can enter the symbol that "
"you want to use to input or display for AM when using a 12-hour clock. The "
"drop-down box provides a list of common symbols for your currently selected "
"language to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>PM symbol</guilabel> text box you can enter the symbol that "
"you want to use to input or display for PM when using a 12-hour clock. The "
"drop-down box provides a list of common symbols for your currently selected "
"language to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Long date format</guilabel> text box you can enter the "
"format that you want to use to input and display long dates. The format "
"entered is a combination of special codes representing date components and "
"literal text used to separate the date components. The special date "
"component codes are listed below. You can set the format to any combination "
"of date components you like, but you should always include at least enough "
"components to uniquely identify a day in the year, &eg; a month and day, to "
"allow you to input dates that are not ambiguous. If you don't include a year "
"component then the current year will be used. The drop-down box provides a "
"list of common date formats in your currently selected language to choose "
"from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>YYYY</parameter> - The year with century as a decimal number "
"(0000-9999)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>YYYY</parameter> - Ova godina sa stoljećem kao decimalni broj "
"(0000-9999)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>YY</parameter> - The year without century as a decimal number "
"(00-99)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>YY</parameter> - Ova godina bez stoljeća kao decimalni broj "
"(00-99)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>MM</parameter> - The month as a decimal number (01-12)."
msgstr "<parameter>MM</parameter> -Mjesec kao decimalni broj (01-12)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>mM</parameter> - The month as a decimal number (1-12)."
msgstr "<parameter>mM</parameter> -Mjesec kao decimalni brojr (1-12)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:525
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>MONTH</parameter> - The full month name."
msgstr "<parameter>MONTH</parameter> - Puno ime mjeseca."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>SHORTMONTH</parameter> - The first three characters of the month "
"name."
msgstr "<parameter>SHORTMONTH</parameter> - Prva tri znaka imena mjeseca."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>DD</parameter> - The day of month as a decimal number (01-31)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>DD</parameter> - Broj dana u mjesecu kao decimalni broj(01-31)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>dD</parameter> - The day of month as a decimal number (1-31)."
msgstr "<parameter>dD</parameter> -Dan mjeseca kao decimalni broj(1-31)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>WEEKDAY</parameter> - The full weekday name."
msgstr "<parameter>WEEKDAY</parameter> -Puno ime dana."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>SHORTWEEKDAY</parameter> - The first three characters of the "
"weekday name."
msgstr "<parameter>SHORTWEEKDAY</parameter> - Prva tri znaka punog imena."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>ERAYEAR</parameter> - The Era Year in local format (&eg; 2000 AD)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>ERAYEAR</parameter> -Era godine u lokalnom formatu(&eg; 2000 AD)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>SHORTERANAME</parameter> - The short Era Name (&eg; AD)."
msgstr "<parameter>SHORTERANAME</parameter> - Kratko ime ere (&eg; AD)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>YEARINERA</parameter> - The Year in Era as a decimal number (&eg; "
"2000)."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>YEARINERA</parameter> - Godina u eri u decimalno broju (&eg; "
"2000)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>DAYOFYEAR</parameter> - The Day of Year as a decimal number."
msgstr "<parameter>DAYOFYEAR</parameter> - Dan u godini kao decimalni broj."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>ISOWEEK</parameter> - The ISO Week as a decimal number."
msgstr "<parameter>ISOWEEK</parameter> - ISO sedmica kao decimalni broj."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>DAYOFISOWEEK</parameter> - The Day of the ISO Week as a decimal "
"number."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>DAYOFISOWEEK</parameter> -Dan u ISO sedmici kao decimalni broj."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Short date format</guilabel> text box you can enter the "
"format that you want to use to input and display short dates. This is in the "
"same format as the <guilabel>Long date format</guilabel>, please read that "
"section for more details. The drop-down box provides a list of common date "
"formats in your currently selected language to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Digit set</guilabel> drop down box lists digit sets which may "
"be used instead of Arabic digits when displaying dates and times. If you "
"select a digit set other than Arabic, it will be applied only to numbers "
"which appear in a language context that uses that digit set while Arabic "
"digits are still going to be used elsewhere, &eg; Arabic-Indic digits will "
"be applied to Arabic but not to American English."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other"
msgstr "Ostalo"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, you can select how other options are displayed. The defaults "
"are selected automatically based on the country which is currently selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Page size</guilabel> drop-down box you can choose the page "
"size to use as the default for new documents, &eg; in KWord. Note that this "
"setting does not affect your default paper size in the print dialog, to set "
"that you need to use the Printers module of the &kde; &systemsettings;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Measurement system</guilabel> drop-down box you can choose "
"the measurement system to use, either metric or imperial."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Byte size units</guilabel> drop-down box you can choose the "
"unit system to use when displaying numbers counted in bytes. Traditionally "
"<quote>kilobytes</quote> meant units of 1024 instead of the metric 1000 for "
"most but not all byte sizes. To reduce confusion you can choose which system "
"you prefer. The available unit systems are listed below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <parameter>IEC Units</parameter> standard is always in multiples of 1024."
msgstr "<parameter>IEC Units</parameter> standard je uvijek u produktu1024."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <parameter>Metric Units</parameter> standard is always in multiples of "
"1000."
msgstr "<parameter>IEC Units</parameter> standard je uvijek u produktu 1000."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <parameter>JEDEC Units</parameter> standard uses the traditional units "
"used in &kde; 3.5 and some other operating systems."
msgstr ""
